1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,340
Slide 16 tackles the greatest curse in conversational AI: "OVERCOMING AMNESIA: The Dual-Memory Engine!"

2
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,939
AI amnesia is so frustrating!

3
00:00:10,939 --> 00:00:21,430
You spend an hour explaining your project's coding standards to a chatbot, and the second the chat session ends, it forgets everything and you have to start from scratch tomorrow!

4
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:25,716
That's because raw LLMs are completely stateless!

5
00:00:25,716 --> 00:00:30,970
Look at how Spark OS solves this with our 3-tier memory hierarchy on screen:

6
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:36,203
Tier 1: In-memory RAM for immediate active scratchpad reasoning.

7
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:44,330
Tier 2: Relational SQLite storing structured facts—client names, past decisions, project deadlines, and transaction IDs!

8
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:53,770
And Tier 3: Vector Embeddings for semantic similarity search across years of historical reports and transcripts in 80 milliseconds!

9
00:00:54,670 --> 00:01:08,230
When a new event arrives, the agent queries SQLite for structured facts, searches vector memory for similar historical cases, and reconstructs full multi-year context in under 100 milliseconds!

10
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:14,340
That is how your avatar gains institutional memory that gets smarter every single day!

